From 3aed8aa40d01d1affd2b55b107b48878d4b06eab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craig Bradney <mrb@scribus.info>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 20:00:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] #17476: Automatic detection of page size format <nitramr> 1.
 Page templates are now loaded from external files. 2. Users can create and
 delete their own templates within the "New Document" dialog. 3. System
 templates are separated from user-generated templates and cannot be modified
 via the UI. 4. Templates support the following values: Width, Height,
 Orientation, Layout, Binding Direction, Margins, and Bleeds. 5. Page
 templates support `legacyNames` used in older Scribus files. 6. Page names
 are localized directly within the template files. Localization is optional;
 names such as "A4" do not require translation. 7. Pages are no longer
 identified by hardcoded IDs, but rather by their dimensions.

